<component type="desktop-application">
  <id>com.sparkybin.Browser</id>
  <metadata_license>CC0-1.0</metadata_license>
  <name>SparkyBin Browser</name>
  <summary>Browse the web</summary>
  <description>
    <p>
      SparkyBin Browser features tight integration with the desktop and a
      simple and intuitive user interface that allows you to focus on your web
      pages. If you’re looking for a simple, clean, beautiful view of the web,
      this is the browser for you.
    </p>
  </description>
  <screenshots>
    <screenshot type="default">
      <caption>A browser window</caption>
      <image>https://github.com/camroybal/SparkyBin-Browser/raw/HEAD/data/screenshot.png</image>
    </screenshot>
  </screenshots>
  <update_contact>https://github.com/camroybal/SparkyBin-Browser/issues</update_contact>
  <kudos>
    <kudo>AppMenu</kudo>
    <kudo>HiDpiIcon</kudo>
    <kudo>ModernToolkit</kudo>
    <kudo>SearchProvider</kudo>
    <kudo>UserDocs</kudo>
  </kudos>
  <project_group>SparkyBin</project_group>
  <project_license>GPL-3.0+</project_license>
  <!-- developer_name tag deprecated with Appstream 1.0 -->
  <developer_name>SparkyBin</developer_name>
  <developer id="com.sparkybin">
    <name>SparkyBin</name>
  </developer>
  <url type="homepage">https://github.com/camroybal/SparkyBin-Browser</url>
  <url type="bugtracker">https://github.com/camroybal/SparkyBin-Browser/issues</url>
  <url type="vcs-browser">https://github.com/camroybal/SparkyBin-Browser</url>
  <url type="contact">https://github.com/camroybal/SparkyBin-Browser</url>
  <translation type="gettext">sparkybin-browser</translation>
  <provides>
    <binary>sparkybin-browser</binary>
  </provides>
  <launchable type="desktop-id">com.sparkybin.Browser.desktop</launchable>
  <content_rating type="oars-1.1" />
  <recommends>
    <control>keyboard</control>
    <control>pointing</control>
    <control>touch</control>
  </recommends>
  <requires>
    <display_length compare="ge">360</display_length>
  </requires>
  <releases>
    <release date="2026-10-20" version="0.2">
      <description>
        <p>The sidebar is new. It shows either the bookmarks or the open tabs, and a switch at the top of it says which. The bookmarks are in groups, and the groups are the user's to choose and to order in the preferences.</p>
        <p>Fifteen colour palettes are available, named after the projects they come from: Gruvbox, Dracula, Catppuccin, Nord, Tokyo Night, Solarized, One Dark, Rose Pine, Kanagawa, Everforest, Monokai Pro, Ayu Mirage and Poimandres.</p>
        <p>The browser keeps its own sizes now, so that a theme cannot squash it. A theme was previously free to decide that a header bar had no height.</p>
        <p>An installed ad blocker now does something. WebKit has no way to let an extension stop a request by itself, so the browser compiles the filter lists that come with an extension into the rules that WebKit's content blockers understand, and puts them on the pages. It is the arrangement Safari uses, and it is what makes the whole of uBlock Origin's list of filters work here. The lists are compiled once and kept.</p>
        <p>New WebExtension calls: permissions.contains and getAll, runtime.onStartup and onInstalled, browserAction.setTitle and setIcon, tabs.onUpdated and onActivated.</p>
        <p>Fixed a number of crashes in the WebExtension code, all of which took the whole browser down: the JSON quoting helper, the extension's own schemes not being addresses, the extension having no identifier, a missing translation, and a reference to the bookmarks manager that was freed twice.</p>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release date="2026-10-19" version="0.1">
      <description>
        <p>First release of SparkyBin Browser, forked from GNOME Web 51.1.</p>
        <p>Changes relative to upstream 51.1:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Rebranded to SparkyBin Browser, with a new application ID, a new executable name and user data directories that no longer collide with a GNOME Web installation</li>
          <li>WebExtensions are enabled by default</li>
          <li>Fixed a number of crashes, use-after-frees and security issues in the WebExtension implementation, including a JavaScript injection in downloads.search(), a path traversal in downloads.download() and the extension API being handed to cross-origin frames</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
  </releases>
</component>
